<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">throw</ansi>

Hurl a throwable item at all hostile creatures in the room.
The projectile detonates on impact, potentially hitting
every enemy. Throwable items are consumed on use.

Each target is rolled against independently -- some may
dodge while others are caught in the blast. A badly
fumbled throw can backfire and hit you instead.

Throwable items include grenades crafted through alchemy:
  <ansi fg="itemname">flashbang</ansi>     Stuns and blinds targets.
  <ansi fg="itemname">firebomb</ansi>      Explodes for physical damage.
  <ansi fg="itemname">toxic flask</ansi>   Releases a lingering toxic cloud.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">throw flashbang</ansi>

Requires being in combat. Shares a cooldown with other
special moves (bash, trip, kick). Uses the
<ansi fg="skill">Skullduggery</ansi> skill and progresses
<ansi fg="stat">Dexterity</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Aging and Storage:</ansi>

  Grenades age over time like potions. Fresh grenades work
  at baseline strength, while aged grenades become more
  potent before eventually declining and spoiling.

  Store grenades in your <ansi fg="itemname">bandolier</ansi> for safety!
  Spoiled grenades in the bandolier are safely ejected to
  the ground. Spoiled grenades left in your backpack risk
  detonating when you rummage through your belongings.

  Use <ansi fg="command">sort</ansi> to move grenades into your bandolier.

